      "message": "This is no longer as clean/clever as the original version, but it also doesn\u0027t access freed memory, and it\u0027s still pretty easy to reason about.\n\nI can picture a more elaborate version of the original (that avoids adding state), but I think the algorithm might be more trouble than it\u0027s worth:\n\n  - Iterate over the MCRecs in reverse order\n  - For any that have a layer, change the device pointer to the next (parent) record\u0027s device, then reset the layer pointer\n  - Then reset the layer pointer\n \n ... actually, that wouldn\u0027t work either, if you had saveLayer(), followed by save(). I think you\u0027d just want to update EVERY MCRec\u0027s device pointer to the base device?",
